WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.640
You hear their footsteps coming down&nbsp;
the halls. Or are those your own?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:10.080
Can you even tell the difference? You can tell&nbsp;
they’re getting closer and you can feel the hate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.080 --> 00:00:16.160
the rage. You turn, shaking, and finally&nbsp;
see them standing right in front of you.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.320
But in that moment, you might as&nbsp;
well be looking into a mirror.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:27.040
And who knows? Perhaps you are. You just don’t&nbsp;
seem to remember having so many reflections...

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:30.720
Have you ever heard the saying “You&nbsp;
are your own worst enemy?” Of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:36.080
it isn’t usually meant literally. But what if&nbsp;
it was? What if you had to fight a monster…that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.320
was you? All of your flaws are reflected&nbsp;
back at you. Your strengths, your weaknesses,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.160
your deepest fears, with no way to escape&nbsp;
except a battle to the death. Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:53.760
you’re not making it out alive. It’s just a&nbsp;
matter of which version of you survives. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.760 --> 00:01:00.480
this isn’t a thought experiment. No, according to&nbsp;
the findings of the SCP Foundation, it’s very much&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:08.240
a reality. There is a place where this nightmare&nbsp;
comes to life, and it is known as SCP-1919.

00:01:08.240 --> 00:01:13.840
SCP-1919 is a hotel and converted&nbsp;
mansion, built in the early 20th century.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.840 --> 00:01:17.360
From the outside, it looks pretty much&nbsp;
like it did when it was first built,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:20.560
and it almost looks like a&nbsp;
comfortable place to stay…&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:25.360
if you ignore the eastern side of the building&nbsp;
that has sunk partially into the ground.

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:32.320
The inside, however, is a different story, where&nbsp;
it’s clear the ravages of time have taken their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:38.720
toll. The floorboards and ceilings are rotting,&nbsp;
collapsing in on themselves, and the rooms are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:44.720
filled with debris. It’s deadly enough to explore&nbsp;
the hotel for these reasons alone, but this is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:50.400
only the beginning of the danger for a person&nbsp;
inside. In order to determine just how dangerous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:56.240
it is for either one person or group to enter the&nbsp;
structure, the SCP Foundation planned a series of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.240 --> 00:02:01.920
research expeditions into the abandoned building,&nbsp;
led by Foundation scientist Dr. Limkiewicz.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:06.480
The first expedition seemed relatively&nbsp;
normal, at least it did at the start.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:12.320
A 39-year-old Caucasian D-Class male known as&nbsp;
D7 was sent into the structure with a camera&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:18.800
and a communications system, guided remotely by&nbsp;
Dr. Limkiewicz, or Dr. L, and another operative,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:25.600
a former head of the MTF Tau-11 “Youth Hostiles”&nbsp;
who is referred to in this file only as T11.

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:30.400
When he arrived at the building, D7 was&nbsp;
unable to get inside through the front door&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:35.120
or windows. After several minutes of trial&nbsp;
and error, he was finally able to get in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:40.000
through the western entrance. Dr. L picked&nbsp;
up a strange, high-pitched whistling noise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:46.000
upon D7’s entrance into the building, but it&nbsp;
quickly faded away and was disregarded by T11.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:50.880
D7 discovered a torn painting, a&nbsp;
portrait of a young woman with red hair.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:55.440
Next to the portrait, shallow scratches&nbsp;
could be seen in the wall, the floor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.440 --> 00:03:01.200
and parts of the ceiling. Suddenly, D7 ducked&nbsp;
into a hiding place, alarmed. He, and the other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:07.840
two operatives listening to his audio feed could&nbsp;
hear heavy breathing… and it didn’t belong to D7.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:12.960
Dr. L recommended that D7 evacuate the&nbsp;
building at this sign of another entity inside,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:19.040
but T11 overruled, ordering him to disregard&nbsp;
that instruction and continue his investigation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.040 --> 00:03:23.600
D7 was told to stay at a safe distance&nbsp;
from whatever was inside with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.600 --> 00:03:28.880
and attempt to capture it on video. D7 turned&nbsp;
off his flashlight in order to better hide, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.880 --> 00:03:34.400
T11 commanded that he turn it back on. Whatever&nbsp;
was caught in its beam of light was difficult for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:40.640
the camera to see, but it threw D7 into a panic&nbsp;
and he began to run in the opposite direction.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:45.840
When prompted to explain what he&nbsp;
saw, D7 simply said: “It was me!”

00:03:45.840 --> 00:03:51.200
D7 ran through the dark, panting with fear&nbsp;
and exertion. Unable to see where his feet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:55.120
were landing, he tripped over something&nbsp;
and came crashing onto the ground,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.120 --> 00:04:00.160
dropping the video camera. This allowed the&nbsp;
observing officers to finally see what D7&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.160 --> 00:04:05.920
was so frightened by, and it became&nbsp;
clear just why D7 was so terrified.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:10.240
A man, identical looking to D7,&nbsp;
approached from the end of the hallway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:16.320
making its way toward the real D7. It was&nbsp;
followed by another man who also resembled D7,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:21.120
and another, all running toward the&nbsp;
original. They all looked exactly like him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.120
with a few notable differences. They&nbsp;
were dressed in the same uniform,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.120 --> 00:04:30.560
with the same build and the same features,&nbsp;
but each had something slightly off about him.

00:04:30.560 --> 00:04:34.320
One was missing eyelids,&nbsp;
another had malformed hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:39.040
and the third had its lips fused together&nbsp;
into a fleshy mass beneath its nose.

00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:44.400
Dr. L moved to cut the camera feed, but T11&nbsp;
demanded that it be kept running. D7 couldn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:49.920
be seen by the camera, but the microphone picked&nbsp;
up the sounds of flesh and cloth being torn, along&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:55.680
with pained, panicked screams as the duplicates&nbsp;
set upon him. After a moment, the screaming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:01.440
stopped. Two hours later, the camera was broken,&nbsp;
and the expedition brought to a troubling end.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:07.680
This was the Foundation’s first glimpse at the&nbsp;
creatures inside of SCP-1919, and it was not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:12.240
pretty. It did, however, allow them to begin&nbsp;
understanding the nature of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:17.760
and what happens when a person goes inside.&nbsp;
It appears that when a human enters the hotel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:22.640
several humanoid creatures manifest throughout the&nbsp;
building. These creatures look like the subject,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:27.680
and are equipped with the same clothing or items&nbsp;
that the subject brought inside with them. Though&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:33.520
they are nearly mirror images of the subject, they&nbsp;
are always slightly warped in a variety of ways.

00:05:33.520 --> 00:05:39.040
These have included changes to limb and digit&nbsp;
length, joint mobility, sealed nostrils,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.040 --> 00:05:44.800
lengthened jaws hanging loose and limp, missing&nbsp;
eyelids, and lips that are fused together.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:48.800
These creatures are highly aggressive&nbsp;
toward the structure of the building itself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:54.160
as well as to the subject that they resemble.&nbsp;
They do not, however, attack each other. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.160 --> 00:05:59.520
appear to operate with a hive mind, exhibiting&nbsp;
swarm intelligence like that of an ant colony.

00:05:59.520 --> 00:06:02.240
Once they have been spawned by&nbsp;
the entrance of a new person,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.800
they will not stop until said person&nbsp;
either escapes the building or is killed.

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:11.920
After the unfortunate end to the first expedition,&nbsp;
the Foundation prepped for a second trip inside.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:18.800
This time, three men were sent in with&nbsp;
Dr. L’s guidance, known as D3, D4, and D9.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.800 --> 00:06:23.200
Video cameras were sewn into their clothes to&nbsp;
leave their hands free and to help avoid some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.200 --> 00:06:27.680
of the issues that came up during the first&nbsp;
expedition. This small team was sent in with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:33.600
the orders to terminate the remaining copies of&nbsp;
D7, and further examine the hotel’s interior.

00:06:33.600 --> 00:06:38.640
Upon opening the door to the building, they&nbsp;
were immediately attacked by one of D7’s copies,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:38.640 --> 00:06:42.640
which D9 was able to quickly dispatch&nbsp;
by firing his weapon at its head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:47.520
Next, after a great deal of reluctance,&nbsp;
the three men entered the building where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:52.720
they spotted something unusual inside.&nbsp;
Dr. L was horrified when the camera feed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:57.200
revealed seventeen discarded video&nbsp;
cameras spread across the floor.

00:06:57.200 --> 00:07:00.480
They didn’t have much time to react&nbsp;
to this new discovery, however,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:05.200
because two doubles, one mirroring&nbsp;
D7 and another mirroring D9,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:09.920
emerged from the wall and began to attack.&nbsp;
Dr. L ordered the team to take shelter,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:13.520
then called the team of guards outside of&nbsp;
the hotel’s perimeter. They were ordered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:18.720
to begin an immediate full perimeter lockdown,&nbsp;
preventing the doubles from leaving the hotel.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:23.840
D3, D4, and D9 attempted to make their&nbsp;
way to a safe corner of the building,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:30.080
but found themselves met with a murderous double&nbsp;
at every turn. At this point, Dr. L began to hear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.080 --> 00:07:34.960
an unusual sound over the microphone feed, a&nbsp;
high-pitched whine like that of a dentist’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.960 --> 00:07:40.480
drill. The operatives on the ground couldn’t hear&nbsp;
a thing, but on Dr. L’s end it was deafening.

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:45.360
As the team proceeded deeper into the hotel,&nbsp;
they became overcome with a strange feeling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:50.080
of foreboding. Dr. L ordered them to turn&nbsp;
on their flashlights, but they refused and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:56.240
begged Dr. L to keep quiet. When prompted&nbsp;
to explain, D9 said: “she can hear you.”

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.680
The operatives stopped responding,&nbsp;
but their camera feeds caught a faint,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:03.360
glowing white light coming from&nbsp;
beneath a door. The door opened,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.360 --> 00:08:07.680
and the light flooded the camera, making&nbsp;
the images it captured hard to decipher.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:12.400
Just a few frames of a quick-moving female&nbsp;
silhouette were captured before the cameras&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:19.840
cut to static. The bodies of D3, D4, and D9&nbsp;
were never recovered, nor were their cameras.

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:25.680
A third expedition was also sent into SCP-1919,&nbsp;
but very little is known about what occurred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:30.880
during it. The video transcript is highly&nbsp;
classified and only those present for its events,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:38.800
or approved to research SCP-1919, have access&nbsp;
to it. An update to the SCP-1919 file following&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:43.680
Expedition Three though, indicates that new&nbsp;
information was revealed about the hotel&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:43.680 --> 00:08:48.720
during the excursion. According to the file&nbsp;
update, there is some kind of being at the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:54.880
center of the location which is causing all of&nbsp;
the other creatures, the doubles, to appear.

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:59.040
The only information available about&nbsp;
this being is the use of the word&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:59.040 --> 00:09:05.360
“her” in the official Foundation log about&nbsp;
SCP-1919. This seems to match up with the last&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:11.120
moments of the operatives in Expedition Two,&nbsp;
when they told Dr. L that “she can hear you”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:15.600
and the few frames of a female figure&nbsp;
that were captured by their cameras.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:20.800
Nothing else is known that has been made&nbsp;
available to anyone outside a very select few.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:26.000
Only the original report exists, and all&nbsp;
other copies of it have been destroyed.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:30.880
The Foundation has undertaken special containment&nbsp;
procedures to make sure that none of the entities&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:30.880 --> 00:09:36.000
from inside the hotel escape, whether they are&nbsp;
the “evil twins” spawned by humans entering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:42.240
the building, or the mysterious female being at&nbsp;
the center of the entire disturbing phenomenon.

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:47.840
The Foundation has classified SCP-1919&nbsp;
as Euclid and a two kilometer radius must&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.840 --> 00:09:53.600
be maintained around SCP-1919, with all&nbsp;
roads leading to the building are blocked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:53.600 --> 00:09:58.880
or diverted so that no vehicles are able to&nbsp;
reach it. This perimeter is guarded by a set&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:03.840
of at least forty armed and armored guards&nbsp;
at any given time. As it has been determined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:03.840 --> 00:10:09.120
that the doubles spawned by 1919 are equipped&nbsp;
with whatever the human they are copying has,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:14.480
no one is allowed to enter the hotel&nbsp;
with body armor or weapons of any kind.

00:10:14.480 --> 00:10:18.800
Anyone that approaches the perimeter that&nbsp;
is not part of an official expedition team&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:22.880
will be immediately terminated. No&nbsp;
new expeditions teams are allowed to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:27.120
enter the building unless all doubles&nbsp;
from the previous expedition have been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:32.640
exterminated. In the event that they cannot be&nbsp;
exterminated, enough time must elapse between&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:32.640 --> 00:10:38.000
expeditions that the previous doubles have starved&nbsp;
to death. Though they do not seem to feel hunger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:43.440
the doubles do need to eat to survive, and&nbsp;
will die when left alone for long enough.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:47.520
SCP-1919 has been sealed off&nbsp;
from the rest of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:47.520 --> 00:10:53.840
so that no hapless civilians can wander inside and&nbsp;
find themselves torn to pieces by warped images of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:59.680
themselves. But that comfort turns cold when you&nbsp;
realize that the SCP Foundation still does not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:06.400
understand what causes these doubles to spawn. Is&nbsp;
it scientific? Supernatural? Or something else?

00:11:06.400 --> 00:11:12.080
No one can be certain. Even more inexplicable&nbsp;
is the entity at the center of all this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:16.960
an unknown female presence capable of wreaking&nbsp;
frightening amounts of violence by turning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:22.560
victims’ own images against them. What is the&nbsp;
purpose of these funhouse mirror nightmares?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:27.520
Who is she, what is she, and what does she&nbsp;
want? Currently, the doubles have shown no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.520 --> 00:11:32.800
interest in leaving the hotel except to attack&nbsp;
intruders, and thanks to that fact, as well as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:38.960
the reinforced perimeter outside, these copycats&nbsp;
have not appeared outside of the building itself.

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.120
But what happens if they do escape,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.120 --> 00:11:46.080
or if the entity that controls them decides&nbsp;
to make her home elsewhere? There is no&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:46.080 --> 00:11:51.680
telling what could happen if this dark power is&nbsp;
allowed to move beyond its current containment.

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:56.960
Are you prepared to fight a vision of&nbsp;
yourself, twisted almost beyond recognition,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:01.760
lunging after you with wide bulbous&nbsp;
eyes, unnaturally long arms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:08.320
and a distended jaw hanging down below its&nbsp;
neck? Better hope you never have to find out.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:15.920
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Children -&nbsp;
Ouroboros Cycle” and “SCP-055 - Anti Meme”&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:20.000
for more anomalous curiosities&nbsp;
from the SCP Foundation!

